The '''2026 Merton London Borough Council election''' will take place on 7 May 2026.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-01 |title=Local elections in London will test support for Reform UK and Greens |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c99k0mzj7x8o |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=[[BBC News]] |language=en-GB}}</ref> All 57 members of [[Merton London Borough Council]] will be elected. The elections will take place alongside [[2026 London local elections|local elections in the other London boroughs]] and [[2026 United Kingdom local elections|elections to local authorities across the United Kingdom]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Number of councils that have requested delay to local elections revealed - is yours one of them? |url=https://news.sky.com/story/local-elections-2026-over-a-third-of-councils-offered-a-delay-have-requested-one-is-yours-on-the-list-13494762 |access-date=2026-01-19 |website=Sky News |language=en}}</ref>

== Background ==
In 2022, Labour held control of Merton Council<ref>{{Cite news |title=Merton result - Local Elections 2022 |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/election/2022/england/councils/E09000024 |access-date=2026-01-19 |work=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref> although their leader lost his seat to the Liberal Democrats who became the official opposition on the Council for the first time.<ref>{{cite web |title=Labour unable to celebrate far from perfect Merton win as Lib Dems claim major scalp |url=https://www.swlondoner.co.uk/news/06052022-labour-unable-to-celebrate-far-from-perfect-merton-win-as-lib-dems-claim-major-scalp |access-date=13 February 2026}}</ref>
In January 2026, the pollster Lord Hayward suggested that the Liberal Democrats could mount a significant challenge to Labour in Merton at the 2026 local elections, suggesting the borough was one where the party could potentially take control.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Exclusive: Labour facing 'fierce battles' to keep hold of at least 12 London boroughs in May local elections |url=https://www.standard.co.uk/news/politics/labour-local-elections-may-london-councils-reform-farage-starmer-b1266859.html |access-date=2026-02-13}}</ref>

